  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the quotient of $3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x-1$ divided by ${x}^{2}+x+1?$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}-4x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{2}-5x-5}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $3x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+4.$",
